    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d48">

                <pb facs="0292" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg34"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1769</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-17T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1915, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 10 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>279. Salandra ministry asked to continue seems to point to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">entente</hi> with Triple Entente. War feeling
                    increasing. American note to Germany received here warm approbation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
